{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadderAnchorDominance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadderAnchorDominance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.MinMax","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.degenerate_correction_is_vacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.degenerate_correction_is_vacuous","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L232-L236","doc":"**The one escape, named so the exclusion is not over-claimed.**\n\n`s = 0` does equalise the anchors — by discarding the prediction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.no_anchor_blind_affine_correction_closes_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.no_anchor_blind_affine_correction_closes_gap","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L216-L230","doc":"**No anchor-blind correction closes the gap.**\n\nA further term appended to the ladder that does not itself depend on the anchor\nacts as one affine map `x ↦ s·x + c` on both predictions.  For `s ≠ 0` the two\nstay distinct.  So the residual spread cannot be removed by carrying the\nα-expansion further, nor by any other anchor-independent ingredient; only an\nanchor-*dependent* one can move it.  Cancellation of `s` needs an integral\ndomain, which is carried as an instance rather than hidden in `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.anchor_gap_eq_prediction_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.anchor_gap_eq_prediction_gap","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L206-L214","doc":"**The anchor gap does not depend on the reference value.**\n\nSubtracting the same reference from both predictions cancels: the difference of\nthe residuals *is* the difference of the raw predictions.  So the comparison\nbetween the two anchors is untouched by which CODATA vintage is used — relevant\nbecause the ladder witness scores against one CODATA vintage while\n`alpha-k-per-force-assembly.witness.json` carries another. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.ladder_carriers_transposition_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.ladder_carriers_transposition_stable","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L193-L197","doc":"And both are stable under transposition, so neither integer depends on how\nthe carrier is presented. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.ladder_carrier_crossing_numbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.ladder_carrier_crossing_numbers","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L187-L191","doc":"**The two carriers the ladder names**, computed from the formula:\n`c(T(2,9)) = 9` and `c(T(3,5)) = 10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.crossing_number_needs_no_convention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.crossing_number_needs_no_convention","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L177-L185","doc":"**The contrast, as one statement.**\n\nOn the very same pair, the crossing number agrees under transposition and the\nwrithe does not.  Hence the α_EM ladder's integers need no minimal-strand\nconvention, while the `δ_q` writhe exponent does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.writheTorus_not_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.writheTorus_not_symm","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L170-L175","doc":"**The writhe rule is NOT symmetric.**\n\n`w(T(2,3)) = 3` but `w(T(3,2)) = 4`, for the trefoil either way.  This is the\ndefect that forced the minimal-strand guard `m ≤ p` on\n`torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.md` and on `rosso_jones_three_strand_delta_q.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.crossingNumberTorus_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.crossingNumberTorus_symm","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L161-L168","doc":"**The crossing number is symmetric.**\n\n`T(p,q)` and `T(q,p)` are the same knot, and this formula assigns them the same\ninteger — with no choice of presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.writheTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.writheTorus","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L158-L159","doc":"The writhe rule the `δ_q` decoration uses: `w(T(m,p)) = (m−1)p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.crossingNumberTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.crossingNumberTorus","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L155-L156","doc":"The crossing number of the torus knot `T(p, q)`: `min (p(q−1)) (q(p−1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.three_mul_of_isGenusTerm_four_of_four_cancellable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.three_mul_of_isGenusTerm_four_of_four_cancellable","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**The converse, with its hypothesis named** (`_of_` per the conditional-lemma\nconvention): recovering `3·p·T = 2` from the ladder relation requires cancelling\n`4`, which fails in characteristic 2.  The hypothesis is carried explicitly\nrather than hidden in a `Field` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.isGenusTerm_four_of_three_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.isGenusTerm_four_of_three_mul","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L127-L138","doc":"**The closed form `2/(3p)` satisfies the relation** — stated as the cleared\nhypothesis `3·p·T = 2`, so the implication holds over any commutative ring with\nno invertibility assumption whatever.\n\nThis is the direction that is actually used: given the closed form, it *is* the\ngenus term.  The converse needs `4` to be cancellable and is therefore stated\nseparately below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.isGenusTerm_four_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.isGenusTerm_four_iff","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L116-L125","doc":"**At the Bring genus `g = 4` the defining relation reads `12·p·T = 8`.**\n\n`4` is not a fitted parameter: it is the genus of Bring's surface.  Division-free\nand characteristic-free — an iff over any commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.IsGenusTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaEM.FormLadder.IsGenusTerm","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlphaEM/FormLadderAnchorDominance.lean#L105-L114","doc":"`T` is *the* genus term at genus `g` (with `p` standing for `π`) exactly when\nit satisfies the ladder's defining relation, stated **cleared of denominators**:\n`4·p·(g−1)·T = 2·g`.\n\nWriting it this way — rather than as `T = 2g/(4p(g−1))` — costs nothing and buys\neverything: it needs no `p ≠ 0`, no `g − 1 ≠ 0`, and **no characteristic\nhypothesis**, so it holds over an arbitrary commutative ring.  A quotient form\nwould force `4 ≠ 0`, i.e. would silently exclude characteristic 2. ","signatureChunk":0}]}